    <div class="ug-callout ug-callout-tip" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        <strong>New to QA Review Studio?</strong> The <a href="/getting-started" class="ug-inline-link">Recommended Workflow</a> page guides you through the platform phase by phase. This User Guide is reference documentation — use it to look up specific features and how they work.
    </div>

    <!-- ── Section 1: Overview ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="overview" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">Overview</h2>
        <p class="ug-section-lead">QA Review Studio is a quality engineering platform focused on <strong>Specification Driven Development (SDD)</strong> — connecting governance rules, requirements, implementation plans, and tasks in a single traceable, governable workflow that spans the full delivery lifecycle.</p>

        <div class="ug-cap-grid">
            @foreach (var cap in CoreCapabilities)
            {
                <div class="ug-cap-card">
                    <div class="ug-cap-icon" aria-hidden="true">@cap.Icon</div>
                    <div class="ug-cap-name">@cap.Name</div>
                    <div class="ug-cap-desc">@cap.Desc</div>
                </div>
            }
        </div>

        <h3 class="ug-subsection-title">Who uses it?</h3>
        <div class="ug-audience-grid">
            @foreach (var (Role, Desc) in Audiences)
            {
                <div class="ug-audience-card">
                    <div class="ug-audience-role">@Role</div>
                    <div class="ug-audience-desc">@Desc</div>
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 2: Core Concepts ───────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="concepts" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">Core Concepts</h2>
        <p class="ug-section-lead">Understanding the four artifact types and the analysis categories that operate across them.</p>

        <h3 class="ug-subsection-title">Artifacts</h3>
        <p>QA Review Studio governs quality across four distinct artifact types. Each artifact is a structured markdown document loaded into the platform for analysis.</p>

        <div class="ug-concept-grid">
            @foreach (var a in ArtifactConcepts)
            {
                <div class="ug-concept-card">
                    <div class="ug-concept-name">@a.Name</div>
                    <div class="ug-concept-file ug-fd-mono">@a.File</div>
                    <div class="ug-concept-desc">@a.Desc</div>
                    <div class="ug-concept-feature">Primary feature: <a href="@a.Route" class="ug-inline-link">@a.Feature</a></div>
                </div>
            }
        </div>

        <h3 class="ug-subsection-title">Analysis</h3>
        <p>Four analysis categories work across the artifact set. Each category answers a distinct governance question.</p>

        <div class="ug-concept-grid">
            @foreach (var a in AnalysisConcepts)
            {
                <div class="ug-concept-card">
                    <div class="ug-concept-name">@a.Name</div>
                    <div class="ug-concept-question"><em>@a.Question</em></div>
                    <div class="ug-concept-desc">@a.Desc</div>
                    <div class="ug-concept-feature">Feature: <a href="@a.Route" class="ug-inline-link">@a.Feature</a></div>
                </div>
            }
        </div>

        <h3 class="ug-subsection-title" id="glossary">Glossary</h3>
        <p>Common terms used throughout QA Review Studio and its documentation.</p>
        <div class="ug-concept-grid">
            @foreach (var g in Glossary)
            {
                <div class="ug-concept-card">
                    <div class="ug-concept-name">@g.Term</div>
                    <div class="ug-concept-desc">@g.Definition</div>
                </div>
            }
        </div>

        <h3 class="ug-subsection-title">AI Review</h3>
        <p>AI Review features augment the deterministic analysis layer with AI-powered advisors and readiness summaries.</p>
        <div class="ug-concept-grid">
            <div class="ug-concept-card">
                <div class="ug-concept-name">AI Change Review</div>
                <div class="ug-concept-question"><em>Are AI-generated changes aligned to the spec?</em></div>
                <div class="ug-concept-desc">AI-assisted review of implementation changes for alignment, quality, and risk. Use after AI generates or modifies implementation work.</div>
                <div class="ug-concept-feature">Feature: <a href="/ai-change-auditor" class="ug-inline-link">AI Change Review</a></div>
            </div>
            <div class="ug-concept-card">
                <div class="ug-concept-name">QA Readiness</div>
                <div class="ug-concept-question"><em>Is the feature ready for release?</em></div>
                <div class="ug-concept-desc">Executive readiness assessment combining all analysis outputs into scored gates. Use at the end of the analysis chain before a release or major milestone.</div>
                <div class="ug-concept-feature">Feature: <a href="/ai-qa-auditor" class="ug-inline-link">QA Readiness</a></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 3: Feature Matrix ───────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="features" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">Full Feature Matrix</h2>
        <p class="ug-section-lead">Every feature at a glance — what it does, what it takes, what it produces, and when to reach for it.</p>

        <div class="ug-table-scroll">
            <table class="ug-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Section</th>
                        <th>Feature</th>
                        <th>Purpose</th>
                        <th>Input</th>
                        <th>Output</th>
                        <th>When To Use</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (var f in AllFeatures)
                    {
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="ug-area-badge ug-area-@f.AreaKey">@f.Area</span></td>
                            <td class="ug-td-feature"><a href="@f.Route" class="ug-inline-link">@f.Name</a></td>
                            <td>@f.Purpose</td>
                            <td class="ug-td-mono">@f.Input</td>
                            <td>@f.Output</td>
                            <td>@f.WhenToUse</td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 4: SDD Workflow ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="workflow" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">SDD Workflow</h2>
        <p class="ug-section-lead">The seven-phase governance workflow — from constitution review to quality &amp; readiness sign-off.</p>

        <div class="ug-core-flow-layout">
            <div class="ug-core-flow">
                <div class="ug-flow-node ug-flow-primary">1 · Constitution Review</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-conn">↓</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-node ug-flow-primary">2 · Specification Review</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-conn">↓</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-node ug-flow-primary">3 · Implementation Planning</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-conn">↓</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-node ug-flow-primary">4 · Traceability &amp; Governance</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-conn">↓</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-node ug-flow-primary">5 · Implementation Review</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-conn">↓</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-node ug-flow-primary">6 · Quality &amp; Readiness</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-conn">↓</div>
                <div class="ug-flow-node ug-flow-secondary">7 · Artifact Publishing (Optional)</div>
            </div>

            <div class="ug-flow-branches">
                <h4 class="ug-branches-title">Phase → Primary Feature</h4>
                <div class="ug-branch-item">
                    <span class="ug-branch-badge">Phase 1</span>
                    <span class="ug-branch-when">Constitution Explorer — review governance rules</span>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-branch-item">
                    <span class="ug-branch-badge">Phase 2</span>
                    <span class="ug-branch-when">Specification Review — extract requirements &amp; AC</span>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-branch-item">
                    <span class="ug-branch-badge">Phase 3</span>
                    <span class="ug-branch-when">Plan Explorer — review ADRs, phases, gates</span>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-branch-item">
                    <span class="ug-branch-badge">Phase 4</span>
                    <span class="ug-branch-when">Artifact Traceability + Constitution Compliance</span>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-branch-item">
                    <span class="ug-branch-badge">Phase 5</span>
                    <span class="ug-branch-when">Implementation Review — task-to-spec alignment</span>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-branch-item">
                    <span class="ug-branch-badge">Phase 6</span>
                    <span class="ug-branch-when">QA Readiness + QA Auditor — readiness gates</span>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-branch-item">
                    <span class="ug-branch-badge">Phase 7</span>
                    <span class="ug-branch-when">QA Artifact Library — publish &amp; reuse assets (optional)</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 5: Typical Workflows ────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="workflows" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">Typical Workflows</h2>
        <p class="ug-section-lead">Common delivery scenarios and the features that support each one.</p>

        <div class="ug-workflow-grid">
            @foreach (var wf in TypicalWorkflows)
            {
                <div class="ug-workflow-card">
                    <div class="ug-workflow-title">@wf.Title</div>
                    <div class="ug-workflow-flow">
                        @for (var i = 0; i < wf.Steps.Length; i++)
                        {
                            <span class="ug-wf-step">@wf.Steps[i]</span>
                            @if (i < wf.Steps.Length - 1)
                            {
                                <span class="ug-wf-arrow">→</span>
                            }
                        }
                    </div>
                    <div class="ug-workflow-desc">@wf.Desc</div>
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 6: Feature Details ──────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="feature-details" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">Feature Details</h2>
        <p class="ug-section-lead">Expand any feature for full details — purpose, inputs, outputs, recommended users, and when to use or avoid it.</p>

        <div class="ug-feature-grid">
            @foreach (var f in AllFeatures)
            {
                var isOpen = _openFeature.Contains(f.Id);
                <div class="ug-feature-card ug-fcard-@f.AreaKey @(isOpen ? "is-open" : "")">
                    <div class="ug-feature-header" @onclick="() => ToggleFeature(f.Id)">
                        <div>
                            <span class="ug-area-badge ug-area-@f.AreaKey">@f.Area</span>
                            <div class="ug-feature-name">@f.Name</div>
                            <div class="ug-feature-purpose">@f.Purpose</div>
                        </div>
                        <button class="ug-expand-btn" aria-expanded="@isOpen.ToString().ToLower()">@(isOpen ? "▲" : "▼")</button>
                    </div>
                    @if (isOpen)
                    {
                        <div class="ug-feature-body">
                            <div class="ug-fd-row">
                                <div class="ug-fd-item">
                                    <div class="ug-fd-label">Input</div>
                                    <div class="ug-fd-value ug-fd-mono">@f.Input</div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="ug-fd-item">
                                    <div class="ug-fd-label">Output</div>
                                    <div class="ug-fd-value">@f.Output</div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="ug-fd-item">
                                <div class="ug-fd-label">Best Used By</div>
                                <div class="ug-fd-roles">
                                    @foreach (var role in f.BestUsedBy)
                                    {
                                        <span class="ug-role-badge">@role</span>
                                    }
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="ug-fd-item">
                                <div class="ug-fd-label">Use When</div>
                                <ul class="ug-fd-list">
                                    @foreach (var when in f.UseWhen)
                                    {
                                        <li>@when</li>
                                    }
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <div class="ug-fd-item">
                                <div class="ug-fd-label">Avoid When</div>
                                <ul class="ug-fd-list ug-fd-list-avoid">
                                    @foreach (var avoid in f.AvoidWhen)
                                    {
                                        <li>@avoid</li>
                                    }
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <a href="@f.Route" class="ug-feature-link-btn">Open @f.Name →</a>
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 7: Where Do I Find This? ────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="where" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">Where Do I Find This?</h2>
        <p class="ug-section-lead">Quick navigation reference — every feature, its purpose, and where it lives in the sidebar.</p>

        <div class="ug-table-scroll">
            <table class="ug-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Feature</th>
                        <th>Purpose</th>
                        <th>Menu Section</th>
                        <th>Route</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (var nav in NavReference)
                    {
                        <tr>
                            <td class="ug-td-feature"><a href="@nav.Route" class="ug-inline-link">@nav.Name</a></td>
                            <td>@nav.Purpose</td>
                            <td><span class="ug-area-badge ug-area-@nav.SectionKey">@nav.Section</span></td>
                            <td class="ug-td-mono">@nav.Route</td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 8: Helpful Scenarios ────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="scenarios" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">Helpful Scenarios</h2>
        <p class="ug-section-lead">Common questions and the features that answer them.</p>

        <div class="ug-scenario-list">
            @foreach (var s in HelpfulScenarios)
            {
                <div class="ug-scenario-item">
                    <div class="ug-scenario-q">@s.Question</div>
                    <div class="ug-scenario-arrow">→</div>
                    <div class="ug-scenario-a">
                        <a href="@s.Route" class="ug-inline-link">@s.Feature</a>
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(s.Note))
                        {
                            <span class="ug-scenario-note"> — @s.Note</span>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 9: Feature Discovery ──────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="discovery" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">Feature Discovery</h2>
        <p class="ug-section-lead">Several powerful analysis views are embedded as tabs inside existing workflows — they do not have dedicated menu items. This section tells you exactly where to find each one and how to activate it.</p>

        <div class="ug-callout ug-callout-tip">
            <strong>Key rule:</strong> Run analysis first, then explore the result tabs. Once analysis completes, switching between tabs does not require re-uploading files — the session is preserved automatically.
        </div>

        <div class="ug-table-scroll">
            <table class="ug-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Feature</th>
                        <th>Found Inside</th>
                        <th>Route</th>
                        <th>How To Access</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Traceability &amp; Coverage</strong></td>
                        <td>Specification Review</td>
                        <td class="ug-td-mono">/extract</td>
                        <td>Analyse a spec → active by default in Analysis Results</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Flow View</strong></td>
                        <td>Specification Review</td>
                        <td class="ug-td-mono">/extract</td>
                        <td>Analyse a spec → click <strong>Flow View</strong> tab in Analysis Results</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Spec Explorer</strong></td>
                        <td>Specification Review</td>
                        <td class="ug-td-mono">/extract</td>
                        <td>Analyse a spec → click <strong>Spec Explorer</strong> tab in Analysis Results</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Risk &amp; Testing</strong></td>
                        <td>Implementation Review</td>
                        <td class="ug-td-mono">/task-alignment</td>
                        <td>Analyse spec.md + tasks.md → click <strong>Risk &amp; Testing</strong> tab in results</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="ug-subsection-title" id="disc-spec-explorer">Spec Explorer</h3>
        <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Spec Explorer is the specification structure and navigation layer. Use it to understand how the specification is organized, browse sections and headings, see which artifacts belong to each section, identify healthy versus unhealthy sections, and navigate into Traceability.</p>
        <p><strong>How to access:</strong> Run analysis on <a href="/extract" class="ug-inline-link">Specification Review</a>, then click the <strong>Spec Explorer</strong> tab in the Analysis Results area.</p>
        <p><strong>When to use:</strong></p>
        <ul class="ug-fd-list">
            <li>Navigating a large or complex specification by structure rather than by extracted item</li>
            <li>Seeing section health, including requirements, tests, clarifications, coverage percentage, and explicit Covered, Partial, or Missing labels</li>
            <li>Understanding User Story ownership without expanding every section</li>
            <li>Opening a requirement or section and jumping into Traceability when coverage needs deeper analysis</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="ug-callout ug-callout-tip">
            <strong>Role clarity:</strong> Traceability &amp; Coverage is for coverage analysis. Flow View is for QA readiness. Spec Explorer is for specification structure and navigation.
        </div>

        <h3 class="ug-subsection-title" id="disc-flow-view">Flow View</h3>
        <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> A QA Readiness dashboard for User Stories. Flow View groups requirements, acceptance tests, success criteria, and implementation tasks by user story — and surfaces gaps, readiness status, and QA Ready scores without requiring manual inspection of each story. It answers: <em>Which User Stories are ready for QA and release?</em></p>
        <p><strong>How to access:</strong> Run analysis on <a href="/extract" class="ug-inline-link">Specification Review</a>, then click the <strong>Flow View</strong> tab in the Analysis Results area.</p>

        <h4 class="ug-feature-title">Story Readiness Status</h4>
        <ul class="ug-fd-list">
            <li><strong>Ready</strong> — requirements, tests, success criteria, and implementation links are present.</li>
            <li><strong>At Risk</strong> — tests exist, but success criteria or implementation links are missing.</li>
            <li><strong>Blocked</strong> — requirements are missing linked acceptance tests.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="ug-subsection-title" id="disc-traceability-view">Traceability &amp; Coverage (Analysis Tab)</h3>
        <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Shows the QA risk picture first: coverage status, missing tests, orphan tests, missing success criteria, missing user story mappings, and relationship gaps. This is the <em>default</em> view shown after analysis.</p>
        <p><strong>How to access:</strong> Run analysis on <a href="/extract" class="ug-inline-link">Specification Review</a>. The Traceability &amp; Coverage tab is active by default in Analysis Results.</p>
        <div class="ug-callout ug-callout-tip">
            <strong>Traceability &amp; Coverage vs. Artifact Traceability:</strong> Traceability &amp; Coverage shows relationships <em>within the specification</em> (requirements to tests). <a href="/artifact-traceability" class="ug-inline-link">Artifact Traceability</a> shows relationships <em>across all four artifacts</em> (Constitution → Spec → Plan → Tasks).
        </div>

        <h4 class="ug-feature-title">Gap Categories</h4>
        <ul class="ug-fd-list">
            <li><strong>Missing User Story:</strong> A coverage requirement is not mapped to a User Story.</li>
            <li><strong>Missing Success Criteria:</strong> A coverage requirement has no linked measurable outcome.</li>
            <li><strong>Missing Tests:</strong> A coverage requirement has no linked acceptance tests.</li>
            <li><strong>Orphan Tests:</strong> A test exists but is not linked to any coverage requirement.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="ug-subsection-title" id="disc-task-explorer">Task Explorer</h3>
        <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Task Explorer is the <strong>Implementation Coverage</strong> workspace. It answers whether the specification is being implemented: which requirements have tasks, which requirements are missing implementation, and where delivery risk exists.</p>
        <p><strong>How to access:</strong> Task Explorer has its own menu item in the REVIEW section (<a href="/task-explorer" class="ug-inline-link">/task-explorer</a>). It is also available as an enriched tab inside Implementation Review after a full analysis.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 10: AI-Assisted Development ─────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="ai-dev" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">AI-Assisted Development</h2>
        <p class="ug-section-lead">QA Review Studio is built for teams using AI to accelerate implementation. The platform helps you maintain quality, traceability, and governance even when velocity is high.</p>

        <div class="ug-ai-flow-row">
            <div class="ug-ai-flow">
                <div class="ug-ai-node">
                    <div class="ug-ai-node-label">Constitution</div>
                    <div class="ug-ai-node-desc">Governance rules, policies, quality standards</div>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-ai-arrow">↓</div>
                <div class="ug-ai-node">
                    <div class="ug-ai-node-label">Specification</div>
                    <div class="ug-ai-node-desc">Requirements, user stories, acceptance criteria</div>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-ai-arrow">↓</div>
                <div class="ug-ai-node">
                    <div class="ug-ai-node-label">Plan + Tasks</div>
                    <div class="ug-ai-node-desc">Architecture decisions, phases, implementation tasks</div>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-ai-arrow">↓</div>
                <div class="ug-ai-node ug-ai-node-terminal">
                    <div class="ug-ai-node-label">Delivery Readiness</div>
                    <div class="ug-ai-node-desc">Go/no-go gate for Development, Testing, and Release</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ug-ai-concepts">
                <div class="ug-ai-concept">
                    <div class="ug-ai-concept-title">Specification-First Development</div>
                    <p>Every task and implementation decision traces back to a requirement. QA Review Studio enforces this by surfacing alignment gaps early using Constitution Compliance and Artifact Traceability.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-ai-concept">
                    <div class="ug-ai-concept-title">Governance</div>
                    <p>Constitution Explorer and Constitution Compliance ensure the project's governance rules are defined, understood, and verified across all artifacts before development begins.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-ai-concept">
                    <div class="ug-ai-concept-title">Traceability</div>
                    <p>Artifact Traceability maintains a complete chain from governance rule to implementation task. QA Auditor identifies missing traceability links with deterministic rule-based findings.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="ug-ai-concept">
                    <div class="ug-ai-concept-title">Readiness</div>
                    <p>QA Readiness and Delivery Readiness aggregate all analysis outputs into scored readiness gates — clearing the team to proceed with confidence through Development, Testing, and Release.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ug-callout ug-callout-tip">
            <strong>Tip:</strong> When using AI to generate tasks from a spec, run Implementation Review immediately after to catch any tasks that introduce undocumented behavior. Then run QA Auditor to surface rule-based quality findings across the full artifact set.
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 11: FAQ ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="faq" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <div class="ug-faq">
            @foreach (var faq in AllFaq)
            {
                var isOpen = _openFaq.Contains(faq.Id);
                <div class="ug-faq-item @(isOpen ? "is-open" : "")">
                    <button class="ug-faq-q" @onclick="() => ToggleFaq(faq.Id)">
                        <span>@faq.Question</span>
                        <span class="ug-faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">@(isOpen ? "▲" : "▼")</span>
                    </button>
                    @if (isOpen)
                    {
                        <div class="ug-faq-a">@((MarkupString)faq.Answer)</div>
                    }
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 12: Analysis Ecosystem ─────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="ecosystem" class="ug-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">Analysis Ecosystem</h2>
        <p class="ug-section-lead">How the Analysis features relate to each other and to the full SDD governance workflow.</p>

        <div class="ug-ecosystem-layout">
            <div class="ug-ecosystem-main">
                <h4 class="ug-ecosystem-subtitle">SDD Governance Chain</h4>
                <div class="ug-eco-flow">
                    <div class="ug-eco-node">Constitution Explorer</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-conn">↓</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-node">Specification Review</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-conn">↓</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-node">Plan Explorer</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-conn">↓</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-node">Artifact Traceability</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-conn">↓</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-node">Constitution Compliance</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-conn">↓</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-node">Implementation Review</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-conn">↓</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-node">QA Auditor</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-conn">↓</div>
                    <div class="ug-eco-node ug-eco-terminal">Delivery Readiness</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ug-ecosystem-support">
                <h4 class="ug-ecosystem-subtitle">Supporting Capabilities</h4>
                <div class="ug-support-list">
                    <div class="ug-support-item">
                        <div class="ug-support-name">Spec Drift</div>
                        <div class="ug-support-desc">Detects coverage gaps, orphan tests, and drift as the codebase evolves.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ug-support-item">
                        <div class="ug-support-name">Impact Analysis</div>
                        <div class="ug-support-desc">Estimates regression scope and identifies high-risk changes across the project.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ug-support-item">
                        <div class="ug-support-name">AI Change Review</div>
                        <div class="ug-support-desc">Reviews AI-generated implementation changes for alignment and quality concerns.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ug-support-item">
                        <div class="ug-support-name">QA Readiness</div>
                        <div class="ug-support-desc">AI-assisted executive summary and readiness assessment based on all analysis outputs.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Section 13: About ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="about" class="ug-section ug-about-section">
        <h2 class="ug-section-title">About</h2>
        <div class="ug-about-content">
            <div class="ug-about-block">
                <p class="ug-about-lead">QA Review Studio is a quality engineering platform focused on:</p>
                <ul class="ug-about-list">
                    <li>Specification Driven Development (SDD)</li>
                    <li>Governance from Constitution to Implementation</li>
                    <li>Traceability from requirement to test</li>
